Fix RTL link placement and make "Show more" actually reveal items

Two bugs reported from the rendered page.

- The "Learn more" link on an Arabic item stayed mid-row instead of moving to
  the left edge. The fix was to DELETE a rule rather than add one: the previous
  `.announcement[dir="rtl"] .announcement-more { grid-column: 1 }` pushed the
  link back into the wide `1fr` column. `direction: rtl` already reverses CSS
  Grid's `1fr auto` track order on its own, so the wide copy column lands right
  and the `auto` link column lands left with no override needed. Only the arrow
  flip remains. Measured: RTL link 0px from the section's left edge, LTR link
  1157px from it.

- "Show more" appeared to do nothing. The reveal observer effect depended only
  on `[items]`, but expanding changes `expanded`, which mounts new `.reveal`
  nodes that nothing ever gave `.reveal-visible` to — so they sat at opacity 0
  while the DOM row count grew, making the button look broken. Added `expanded`
  to the dependency array.

Verified with 5 stubbed rows (mixed English/Arabic, some linked): collapsed
shows 3, expands to 5, every item at opacity 1 with reveal-visible, toggle
relabels to "Show less", Arabic link flush left and English flush right.
13/13 unit, typecheck, eslint incl. components/lib, static build, 158/158 QA,
33/33 motion, 21/21 overflow.
